  "risks": [
    {"id": "R1", "risk": "Fault injection (store_unavailable, internal_error, rate_limited) requires reference-impl test hooks. Mitigation: mark these fixtures pending: true if hooks absent; add hooks behind SOX_TEST_FAULTS=1 env in 02-build."},
    {"id": "R2", "risk": "Backpressure thresholds are implementation-tuneable. Mitigation: fixtures use server_config.queue_limit override to pin the threshold deterministically."},
    {"id": "R3", "risk": "Idempotency TTL is implementation-tuneable; sleep-based 'after TTL' tests are slow. Mitigation: server_config.idempotency_ttl_ms = 100ms in fixtures; sleep step 200ms."},
    {"id": "R4", "risk": "Typed channels (registered body schemas) are not yet a first-class spec primitive. Mitigation: server_config.typed_channels map; if adapter does not support, fixture is skipped with a clear message in non-strict mode."},
    {"id": "R5", "risk": "version-negotiation requires the harness to spoof a client supported_versions range. Mitigation: as_client_version step field; HTTP adapter sends X-SOX-Client-Versions header; in-process adapter calls a public set_client_versions()."},
    {"id": "R6", "risk": "delivered_to lifecycle relies on read-then-update semantics; some impls populate eagerly. Mitigation: assert delivered_to is null OR empty list pre-recv (both acceptable per spec), populated post-recv."},
    {"id": "R7", "risk": "100% line coverage on the runner is brittle if it includes adapter stubs for HTTP. Mitigation: split InProcess and HTTP adapters into dedicated modules covered via responses/respx mocks."}
  ],
